    "body": "Hi @oushujun, \nI got similar warning messages for two of the species I am annotating. I wanted to report it here but I am not sure what you mean by 'unique warning lines'. \n\nThe one-line code you wrote in the first message returns this. \n\n```\ncat de_novo_TE_ArrayJob_5621298_1.err | grep TE_SO | sed 's/Warning: //' | awk '{print $1}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -k1,1 -rn\n   2344 PLE\n\ncat de_novo_TE_ArrayJob_5621298_5.err | grep TE_SO | sed 's/Warning: //' | awk '{print $1}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -k1,1 -rn\n    762 PLE/Chlamys\n```\n\n\nIs this all you need? or do you need all lines like this: \n```\nWarning: PLE/Chlamys not found in the TE_SO database, will use the generic term 'repeat_fragment\tSO:0001050' to replace it.\nWarning: PLE not found in the TE_SO database, will use the generic term 'repeat_fragment\tSO:0001050' to replace it.\n\n```\n\n",
